            <ArticleTitle>Acute intermittent porphyria. A perplexing case.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>357-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report the case of a 58-year-old woman affected by polyneuropathy, vegetative disturbances and abdominal pain. A provisional diagnosis of acute intermittent porphyria was made and was confirmed by the increased levels of urinary delta-aminolevulinic acid (ALA) and porphobilinogen (PBG).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
